# Arguments for the hourly cardiac SRM combine (qmirt-cardiac-combine.service).
#
# Copy to cardiac.env and edit; the unit reads it if present, otherwise it uses
# "--latest". No systemctl edit or daemon-reload is needed after changing this
# file, because the timer re-reads it on every run.
#
# Follow whichever campaign is newest on the OSPool mount:
CARDIAC_COMBINE_ARGS=--latest
#
# Pin one campaign, e.g. while an older one is still draining:
# CARDIAC_COMBINE_ARGS=--batch batch_20260909_004729
#
# Pool several submissions of one logical campaign into a single SRM. A campaign
# split across submissions (the 20000-jobs-per-submission limit) lands in several
# batch directories, and --latest only sees the newest, so give them a shared
# --local-dir and run one line per batch:
# CARDIAC_COMBINE_ARGS=--batch batch_A --local-dir /data/fanghan/opengate_sim/data/cardiac_spect/campaign_01
#
# Large campaigns need a tree reduction to stay within memory:
# CARDIAC_COMBINE_ARGS=--latest --shard-count 16
